1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<font color="#FF8040">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.Org</font>

2
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,932
I don't know if that's true…

3
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:16,850
Oh.

4
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:17,809
God dammit.

5
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:20,645
Richard's guys must have tore
a hole in the coop.

6
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:21,980
I'm gonna…

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,190
Okay, honey. Honey, listen.

8
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:28,903
Just sit down, have your coffee,
and… I'll take care of the chickens.

9
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:35,285
We should've just sold to that developer.

10
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,039
Do you really mean that?

11
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:54,137
You know what's killing me?

12
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:59,934
Is that Will's still working with Richard.
Even after he threatened to cut us out.

13
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,856
Maybe he thinks it'll keep him in check.

14
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:07,067
Why? Nothing else does.

15
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:13,573
I'm done with this.

16
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:18,536
I'm not gonna let Richard or anybody else
make decisions about our property.

17
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,371
I'm gonna fix it.

18
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:21,331
How?

19
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:22,832
I have an idea.

20
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:26,461
I don't want to talk about it now,
because it's kind of going,

21
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,713
but if it works,
it will sort all this out.

22
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:31,716
Okay? So just… just give me a couple days.

23
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,634
Okay.

24
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:36,304
I'm gonna go look for
some wire in the garage.

25
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:37,263
Okay.

26
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:40,600
I'm just gonna sit here
and have some coffee.

27
00:01:41,392 --> 00:01:42,477
With my chicken.

28
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:51,152
You watching the University of Texas game?

29
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:55,240
Yeah, they run this combo
of a zone and man-to-man defense.

30
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:56,407
It's gorgeous.

31
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:58,034
Thinking of using it for the Bighorns?

32
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:02,831
Um, actually, I got a meeting
with the UT rep at the college thing.

33
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:04,666
First time they've come out here,

34
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,793
and I kind of wanna
get in their coaching program.

35
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:08,795
I've been trying
to get a feel for their playbook,

36
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:11,631
how they run their offense,
how they run their defense, and just…

37
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:13,216
I'm boring you, aren't I?

38
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:15,510
No. No, it's just, uh…

39
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:19,180
I'm really glad
my little brother's got his mojo back.

40
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:22,016
Please. You're 20 minutes older than me.

41
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:22,976
Okay?

42
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:25,645
Yeah, and every minute counts, kiddo.

43
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:26,980
Stop.

44
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,199
We should go get ready.

45
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:39,159
We got time.

46
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,538
I cannot be late.

47
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:46,291
I have to help set up
all the college fair booths.

48
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:50,295
If it doesn't go smoothly, I won't be able
to focus on our final mock driver's test.

49
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:52,005
Okay. Okay, we'll go.

50
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:53,548
Thank you.

51
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,345
What?

52
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:01,472
Nothing.

53
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:07,520
I… I just…

54
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:11,941
I love you.

55
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:39,719
What you doing?

56
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:45,934
Uh, I'm developing my own video game.
Just working on some designs.

57
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:49,520
Wow, that's pretty amazing. You know that?

58
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:53,107
Yeah, whatever. What do you want?

59
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:56,778
Well, I did just wanna hang out with you,
but now I also want to see your drawings.

60
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:58,071
No, absolutely not.

61
00:03:58,655 --> 00:03:59,739
Come on.

62
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:02,200
Fine.

63
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,202
You get one quick look.

64
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,414
Wow.

65
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:11,876
It's kind of like that, um, new
Quantum Justice movie that just came out,

66
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,670
except a little more fantasy stuff.

67
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:16,256
-You've seen it?
-No. No, I've just read all the books.

68
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:20,134
-What's this guy's name?
-I'm still workshopping him.

69
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,637
He's, like, probably not even gonna be
in the game, so…

70
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:25,598
Too bad. He's my favorite.

71
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:30,228
Shouldn't you be doing something else?

72
00:04:30,311 --> 00:04:32,855
Like, uh, prepping to talk
to the Oklahoma rep tomorrow?

73
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:35,733
Actually, uh, my dad and I
already met with him.

74
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,568
What? How'd it go?

75
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:38,861
Uh,

76
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,280
really well.

77
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:44,200
Like, my dad was… happy.

78
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,201
Hmm.

79
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:47,287
He said he was proud of me.

80
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:51,374
Well, you should celebrate.

81
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:55,378
You know, now that you mention it,
I think I would like to celebrate

82
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:58,589
by going to see Quantum Justice.
Wanna come with?

83
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:00,591
Seriously?

84
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,427
Yeah, you're not working tonight, right?

85
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,346
You're right. I am not.

86
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:09,100
Great. Well, I will see you
at the Mirror Ball at 7:00.

87
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:13,271
Dylan?

88
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:16,024
Is this, like, a date?

89
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,233
What? No way.

90
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,903
Oh no, right, sorry, I…

91
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:23,656
Kiley, Kiley, Kiley, I'm joking.

92
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,284
Do you want it to be?

93
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,578
No.

94
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:30,747
I don't know.

95
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,875
All right, well, maybe we can decide
after the movie?

96
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,295
Deal.

97
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:45,511
So, the last two colleges confirmed.

98
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:50,016
Let's see, and you marked all
the classrooms for the one-on-ones, right?

99
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:52,643
We have a lot of students coming.
We don't want anyone to get lost.

100
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:54,979
-Yeah, no one's gonna miss them.
-Perfect.

101
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:57,899
Okay, and that's the end of my checklist.

102
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:03,529
-So what's wrong? Did we miss something?
-No.

103
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:07,408
-It's not a big deal.
-Is it 'cause there's no Princeton rep?

104
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,369
No, Miss Jacobs said
they'd come next year.

105
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,536
Is it the driver's test?

106
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,497
I've actually been doing okay
in driver's ed.

107
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,749
All I've got to do now is get through
my final mock test,

108
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,459
and I'll be ready for the real one.

109
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,338
-Okay, fine.
-Wha…

110
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:25,301
-It's Alex.
-Oh, I knew it! Okay, what's wrong?

111
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,178
He said he loved me.

112
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:30,139
-Well, didn't he already tell you that?
-It was different this time.

113
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:33,017
I think he means it,
and I think he expects me to say it back.

114
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,811
Well, you do like him, don't you?

115
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:36,938
Yeah, of course, obviously.

116
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:38,564
Well, I don't know what the problem is.

117
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:41,359
I mean, I say I love you to everyone.
Like, all the time.

118
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:45,238
You, Skylar, the lunch lady
that one time we had Oreo cheesecake.

119
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:48,991
It just feels like a big deal after
everything that's happened between us.

120
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,284
Mm, I get that.

121
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,496
Well, it doesn't mean
you'll never get there, right?

122
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,957
Um… right.

123
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,167
I gotta go.

124
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,837
-Guys, the sign's upside down.
-Jackie, where are you going?

125
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,463
All right, so we'll start at the, uh…

126
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:04,966
Let's put a pin in this for now.
I'll get back to you.

127
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:06,008
Hi.

128
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:09,429
So you know your guys tore a hole
in our chicken coop this morning?

129
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:12,765
I'm so sorry, Mom. It won't happen again.

130
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,476
It's this pressure to rush
that's making us a little sloppy.

131
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,437
Well, it's fine now
'cause your dad fixed it.

132
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,814
But that pressure…
that pressure's not coming from us.

133
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:20,982
Yeah, I know that.

134
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,986
I really don't like
that Richard's pushing you so hard.

135
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,864
It'll be okay. It's just…

136
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:31,284
I have to figure out
how to get him to listen to me.

137
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:34,829
-I thought you were working together.
-Yeah, me too.

138
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:39,417
Sorry. I gotta get back.

139
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:49,218
Okay, so right now we have
all of these colleges confirmed.

140
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:50,303
Okay, nice.

141
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:51,804
That's a good list.

142
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,931
-In 15-minute intervals--
-Are there anymore…

143
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:55,016
-Jackie?
-Yeah.

144
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:58,186
-Hi.
-Hi.

145
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:03,483
-Oh, so…
-Uncle Richard, this is Grace.

146
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:04,734
And you remember Skylar?

147
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:06,402
Yeah, it's nice seeing you again.

148
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:08,446
I was just stopping by
to pick up something to go,

149
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:12,116
but since you're here, you wanna
grab some dessert from the Lark?

150
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:15,328
Sorry, we've really got to get ready
for this college fair tomorrow.

151
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:16,287
Another time.

152
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,413
For sure.

153
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:18,915
It was nice seeing you both.

154
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:19,999
-You too.
-Yeah.

155
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,087
Okay.

156
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,464
Georgetown?

157
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,007
-Focus. Focus. Focus.
-Anyways…

158
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:33,304
-Grace! You're getting mean.
-Didn't say anything! You said it.

159
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,558
His Girl Friday or It Happened One Night.

160
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:40,102
Oh, It Happened One Night, obviously.

161
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:41,979
The Walls of Jericho scene.

162
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:44,607
Me and my grandma used to watch it
every year for her birthday.

163
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:45,900
It was her favorite movie.

164
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:49,028
Clark Gable's performance
is just perfection.

165
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:52,490
You know, now that we've got
our SATs back and everything,

166
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,909
we should practice our monologues.

167
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:57,870
Yeah, I can help you.

168
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,497
I'd help with yours too.

169
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:03,084
We could maybe think
of a scene to do together.

170
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:05,670
Or maybe we could even
coordinate our applications.

171
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:07,505
-Danny.
-Yeah?

172
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:09,924
I'm not applying to Tisch.

173
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:12,218
Okay. Yeah, that's cool.

174
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:14,887
We… we don't have to go to the same place.

175
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:17,598
Juilliard is tough,
but after that summer program--

176
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:20,393
I'm gonna go to community college
here in Silver Falls.

177
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:23,980
Oh.

178
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:27,024
Yeah, that way I can avoid
getting into crazy debt

179
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:30,528
and maybe transfer to a four-year
after a couple years to major in business.

180
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:33,531
Yeah, but you… you love acting.

181
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:36,284
-You shouldn't give it up.
-I'm not giving up.

182
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:39,745
I've been thinking about this
since middle school. I have a plan.

183
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:44,417
Okay, but plans can change,
and you'd be an amazing actor.

184
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,711
I did one play.

185
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:48,963
In high school.

186
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:50,798
Did I enjoy it?

187
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:52,633
Yeah, but I'm not gonna be an actor.

188
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:55,595
Like you said, you did one play,
and you were great.

189
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:59,265
Okay, so maybe if you did another one,
you'd realize that is what you want.

190
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:02,435
I know what I don't want.

191
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:06,230
A boyfriend who thinks he knows
what I want better than I do.

192
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,108
I'm gonna go home.

193
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:11,777
Okay, yeah, I'll drive you.

194
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:12,695
I can walk.

195
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:24,373
Alex, if I wanted to learn
how to play Confederacy of the Gods,

196
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:25,708
could you help me?

197
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,211
Uh, sure.

198
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:35,217
Just so you know, it took Kiley
and me over 100 hours just to get ranked.

199
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:38,679
-I have no idea what that means.
-Yeah, exactly.

200
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:40,973
Why would you even wanna play?

201
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:43,643
You've never been into video games.

202
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,811
Mm, well, Zach's a big fan.

203
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:47,188
Zach's a big fan.

204
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:51,025
Yeah, and apparently
this new expansion pack came out.

205
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:54,278
-I want to see what he's raving about.
-A new expansion pack came out?

206
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:59,950
-How did I miss that?
-I mean, do you even play anymore?

207
00:11:00,701 --> 00:11:03,788
Well, you know, I haven't had much time.

208
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:06,832
Yeah, you're kind of like
a totally different person now.

209
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,044
Zach thinks you're going through a phase.

210
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:13,047
Whatever. What would he know?

211
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:18,636
Anyway, at least I'm changing for myself
and not for somebody else.

212
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:20,971
Oh, I didn't say it like it's a bad thing.

213
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:23,849
Wait, are you talking about me?

214
00:11:24,975 --> 00:11:30,606
If I'm changing, I feel like it's because
I'm becoming, like, more myself.

215
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,442
Like Zach's helping me be
the best version of myself.

216
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,986
Is he? 'Cause…

217
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:42,034
it seems like
it's all about what Zach likes,

218
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:45,121
what Zach thinks, what Zach does,

219
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:47,373
what Zach wants.

220
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:49,583
That's not true.

221
00:11:52,461 --> 00:11:54,338
If you're not using your account,
can I have it?

222
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:55,464
Hell no.

223
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:00,344
Oh my God, shut up.

224
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:05,558
-Hi.
-Hey, you. Can you talk?

225
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:06,517
Yeah.

226
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,311
-Oh my God.
-No, I'll just leave.

227
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:13,899
Ay, ay, ay.

228
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:37,214
Okay, tell me are you a cookie dough bites
or a sour gummy worm kind of gal?

229
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,175
Oh, both. And then some.

230
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:43,095
You know you're not supposed to bring
your own snacks, right?

231
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,181
I can't afford the snacks here.

232
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,932
Well, this one's on me.

233
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:49,351
Oh, no, no, that's… that's okay.

234
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,188
Come on. When was the last time
you got treated to something?

235
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:56,066
Kiley, I'm going
to be buying candy anyway.

236
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:01,447
I can't remember the last time
I had actual movie theater candy.

237
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:04,074
Most of my work money goes to Grams.

238
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:07,787
Don't your parents send her cash
to take care of you?

239
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:11,916
They've still got the Quantum Justice
themed popcorn buckets.

240
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:15,377
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, we're definitely
getting one of those, right?

241
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:16,712
Um, hey, uh,

242
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:19,215
we'll take two cookie dough bites,
some sour gummy worms,

243
00:13:19,298 --> 00:13:22,384
a large Quantum Justice popcorn,
and a soda?

244
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:23,969
-Yeah.
-Two sodas, please.

245
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,144
Surprise.

246
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:33,604
Hey.

247
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:35,731
-Hey.
-Oh, sorry. I…

248
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:37,691
I gotta get to band practice.

249
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:40,361
What, now?
I thought you had band fourth period.

250
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:45,241
Yeah, but we're working on a new set,
so they'll be waiting for me.

251
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:46,909
Come on, you can skip it.

252
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:50,162
I wanted to take you to breakfast.

253
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:53,332
Um…

254
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:57,336
Yeah, I guess one practice won't hurt.

255
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:01,048
That's my guy.

256
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,094
You comin'?

257
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,228
Thank you.

258
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:23,028
Victoria. Hey. George.

259
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:25,531
Oh, it's so nice
to finally meet you in person.

260
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,116
I know. Yeah, thank you for coming in.

261
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:28,951
Oh, my pleasure.

262
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:32,746
Your artisanal cider is
the highlight of my family's fall.

263
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:33,664
Thank you.

264
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:38,127
I was happy that your ranch
didn't have to close down last year.

265
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,838
And I'm even happier you're considering us

266
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:43,257
as your wine supplier
for your new venture.

267
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:45,759
Well, about that.

268
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:48,721
I actually wanted to talk to you
about another way we could work together.

269
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:50,472
I'm listening.

270
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:53,225
-Can I get you some coffee?
-Sure.

271
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,066
One for you.

272
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,074
-We're so good at this.
-I know.

273
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:12,453
Wait a minute.

274
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:15,331
Oh, did you know they have
a pastry chef from Paris on the faculty?

275
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:17,708
-France?
-Kentucky. But, you know…

276
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:20,920
Well, while you go pursue
your patisserie dreams,

277
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:22,546
I'm set on Georgetown.

278
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,424
They have
a great Indigenous studies working group.

279
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:27,217
Mm. What about you, Jackie?

280
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:29,470
Honestly, I'm just glad
things are going well.

281
00:15:29,553 --> 00:15:30,471
Fair.

282
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:36,685
There weren't supposed to be
any empty booths.

283
00:15:37,561 --> 00:15:38,687
I'll be right back.

284
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:44,568
You're welcome.

285
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,362
Jackie, hey!

286
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:48,781
Thank you so much
for helping put all this together.

287
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:51,867
And your Excel spreadsheets…
a work of genius.

288
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,243
Thanks.

289
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:56,538
But why are there empty booths?
Did something happen?

290
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,207
Some of the colleges had to pull out.

291
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:02,544
Scheduling conflicts, people getting sick,
and just now, car trouble.

292
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,838
It happens. Don't take it to heart.

293
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:05,756
Okay.

294
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:08,592
I'll need your help letting students know
which reps couldn't make it.

295
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,970
-Great. Thank you. I appreciate that.
-Of course.

296
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,722
Hi. Um, is Pat Harris from UT here?

297
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:18,268
Cole, I am so sorry, but Mr. Harris's car
broke down on the way here.

298
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,188
Right. Um…

299
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:24,692
-Yeah. It's… it's okay.
-Cole.

300
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:26,944
Well, well, uh,

301
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:32,866
what if, let's just say, someone who's
good at fixing cars could help Mr. Harris?

302
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:36,829
Maybe even manage to do a one-on-one
about the college while they're there?

303
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,664
Of course, this is all hypothetical.

304
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,958
Obviously, I would never tell
a student to skip school.

305
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:45,421
Yeah, but I… I came with Danny today,
so I can't go anywhere anyways.

306
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,048
Uh… uh…

307
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:50,384
-Take my car.
-Are you serious?

308
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:52,094
It's a stick.
You can drive a stick, right?

309
00:16:52,177 --> 00:16:54,930
-Yes, ma'am.
-Okay. Take these before I change my mind.

310
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:56,181
Be careful with her, Cole.

311
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:59,560
I will call Pat and tell him
that Silver Fall High's best mechanic

312
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:00,519
is on his way.

313
00:17:00,602 --> 00:17:02,855
-Thank you.
-You're welcome. Good luck.

314
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:09,987
Are you okay?

315
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:12,990
This is your chance to stand out
from all the other applicants.

316
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:14,199
You have to go.

317
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:16,118
Okay.

318
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:18,996
Okay. I guess.

319
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:22,374
Good luck.

320
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:29,715
I'm pretty sure the spaces will fill up.
We'll be good.

321
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,009
Wait, Sky, we should try goldsmithing.

322
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:34,136
Imagine me with my own jewelry line.

323
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:35,387
What should I call it?

324
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:37,097
"A little bit of Grace."

325
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,141
-Wait, that's actually sickening.
-I know!

326
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,155
-See you soon.
-Okay.

327
00:17:53,238 --> 00:17:55,199
Should we go somewhere else?

328
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:56,158
No.

329
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,161
Um… you two go ahead.

330
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,081
I wanna talk to Nathan.

331
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:09,797
Okay. Well, this is going well though.

332
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,049
Hey.

333
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:13,467
Hey.

334
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:16,386
So that looks like it's getting serious.

335
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:18,263
Yeah.

336
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:21,850
Who have you managed to interview so far?

337
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:22,893
Just a few.

338
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:24,061
Show me.

339
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:28,899
Okay.

340
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:30,984
Look, Nate.

341
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,946
I believe in honesty in relationships.

342
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:38,117
I think you need to be careful. There are
things you don't know about Zach.

343
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,410
Okay. I'll bite. What things?

344
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:42,204
Things you should ask him about yourself.

345
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,750
Look, all I'm trying to say is,

346
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:49,628
no matter how nice things
may feel right now,

347
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:51,088
don't lose yourself in him.

348
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:52,297
Uh, Skylar.

349
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,675
Okay, fine.

350
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:57,052
In the name of honesty,
are you looking out for me

351
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,262
or are you just jealous?

352
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:01,473
Seems like the jealousy
wasn't totally in my head.

353
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:05,144
But the Nate I knew
wouldn't act like this.

354
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:07,396
Well, I don't know what to tell you.

355
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,648
Maybe you didn't know me
as well as you thought you did.

356
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:14,945
Like I said,

357
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,322
just be careful.

358
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,199
-Okay?
-Okay.

359
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:30,169
Kiles, did you get my text

360
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,254
about the Confederacy of the Gods
expansion pack?

361
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:34,965
Uh, yeah. Sorry. Sorry, I was… I was busy.

362
00:19:35,048 --> 00:19:36,800
Oh. Yeah, sure.

363
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,761
Uh, dinner rush
at Monty's is no joke, right?

364
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:42,472
Actually, I wasn't working. I was out.

365
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,599
Out?

366
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:44,516
Yeah.

367
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:47,394
I… I know it's hard to imagine
that I have other things besides work

368
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:49,563
and video games going on, but I do.

369
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:51,273
-I know that.
-So what is it then?

370
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:53,984
You have some girl problem you want
to emotionally vomit all over me?

371
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:56,820
No, we haven't talked in a while,
and I really wanted to--

372
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,239
Maybe you should ask
one of your rodeo groupies to help you.

373
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,574
I have things to do.

374
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,783
Kiley.

375
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:02,701
Hey.

376
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,203
Uh, everything okay?

377
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,997
Everything's great.
I'll see you later, Alex.

378
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:15,130
-Um, are… are you sure everything's okay?
-Yeah.

379
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,840
Yeah, absolutely.

380
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:20,219
And, um, last night… definitely a date.

381
00:20:20,302 --> 00:20:22,387
-Really?
-Really.

382
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,140
Good.

383
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:29,519
-Oh, it's my grandma. I gotta go.
-Well, can I help?

384
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:33,023
Grams? What is it? Are you okay?

385
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:35,609
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

386
00:20:35,692 --> 00:20:36,526
Okay, bye.

387
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:40,405
Jackie.

388
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,950
Can't wait for this social interaction.

389
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:43,867
What's up?

390
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:49,039
Listen, I don't totally get your whole
pizza voucher PTA things or whatever,

391
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:52,584
but this event is, um,
actually kind of awesome.

392
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:56,046
I mean, who knew I had the grades for
University of Wisconsin-Madison, right?

393
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:59,049
That's great. I'm glad the fair
is opening up some ideas for you.

394
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:02,261
You know what? You would've made
a better class president than Paige.

395
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:05,180
I have a feeling this Hawaii trip
she promised is not gonna happen.

396
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,057
-You think?
-Look, I gotta go.

397
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:10,018
I got a one-on-one with Northwestern.
I'll see you later.

398
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:12,688
Look at this turnout.

399
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:15,607
With all the last-minute sign-ups,
we're completely booked.

400
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:18,944
You know, I wasn't sure enough juniors
would be interested in today,

401
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:20,487
but you have proven me wrong.

402
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:22,698
-It was nothing.
-It wasn't nothing.

403
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:26,326
With your help, we've made these students
feel like they can go anywhere

404
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,327
and be anything.

405
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:31,039
Um, do you have any more
of those maps printed?

406
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:33,250
-I think we ran out.
-There's a pile on my desk.

407
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:34,876
-Great.
-Thank you.

408
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:40,924
Cole?

409
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:50,100
What are you still doing here?
Did you forget something?

410
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:51,184
No.

411
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:52,644
It's just…

412
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:54,646
What?

413
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:58,025
I'm not ready for this.

414
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:01,028
Come on. You're gonna do fine.

415
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:03,363
I've never done anything like this, okay?

416
00:22:03,447 --> 00:22:06,450
My… my interview with Tony
for the auto shop was like,

417
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:08,577
"Hey, I know you like cars.
Come work for me."

418
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:11,038
Sure, but once you're in it, it's easy.

419
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:13,915
What if I say something stupid?

420
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:14,958
You won't.

421
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:19,504
Come with me.

422
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:24,092
I wish I could,
but with the college fair--

423
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:25,302
Please.

424
00:22:25,385 --> 00:22:27,179
I know it's a big ask.

425
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:35,020
Okay.

426
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,900
Yeah, I can leave things
to Grace and Skylar.

427
00:22:41,818 --> 00:22:46,323
So the meteor falling is actually
a catalyst for four different storylines

428
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:49,534
before they all converge…
Well, I don't want to spoil it.

429
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:53,747
I mean, I… I have to read this.
Can I borrow it when you're done?

430
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:55,082
Yeah, sure.

431
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:55,999
Cool.

432
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:00,337
-I'll see you later, Alex.
-See ya.

433
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:07,469
What were you even talking about?

434
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:10,055
Oh, this new sci-fi series.

435
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:13,016
-Basically, after this meteor--
-No wonder they looked so bored.

436
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,017
All right.

437
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:16,812
Where are you going?

438
00:23:16,895 --> 00:23:17,729
Look,

439
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:23,485
I don't know what's up with you lately,
but if you're gonna be a dick, I'm out.

440
00:23:23,568 --> 00:23:25,654
Alex, wait.

441
00:23:26,321 --> 00:23:27,531
It's Skylar.

442
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:34,955
Um…

443
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:38,500
He just, like, gave me
this vague-ass warning about Zach,

444
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:40,252
and I'm, like, freaking out.

445
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:42,879
-Maybe he's got a point.
-What? I mean…

446
00:23:43,588 --> 00:23:45,924
Okay, so, like,
I missed one band practice.

447
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:48,093
-And I wanna do the things he likes, but--
-Hold up.

448
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:50,095
You missed band practice,

449
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:52,431
and you're trying to get into video games?

450
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:54,933
Yeah, but isn't it good to try new things?

451
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:56,184
Yeah.

452
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:59,729
As long as you're not giving up things
you like and only doing what he wants.

453
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:02,274
Okay, I don't know. Maybe you're right.

454
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:05,360
Maybe I should just talk to him,
ask him what Skylar means?

455
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:06,278
Yeah.

456
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:09,656
And stop skipping band practice.

457
00:24:11,908 --> 00:24:14,286
Just leave the car in neutral

458
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:16,455
And meet me after dark

459
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:18,415
The spot around the corner…

460
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:21,710
Next question.
How would you describe yourself?

461
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,421
Let's see.

462
00:24:24,921 --> 00:24:26,965
Charming, good-looking…

463
00:24:27,048 --> 00:24:29,885
Okay. Good to see
you got your confidence back.

464
00:24:29,968 --> 00:24:33,221
I guess as a fixer, you know?

465
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:36,057
I look at something, like a car,

466
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:39,936
see what it needs,
and find a way to fix it.

467
00:24:41,938 --> 00:24:43,607
I just wish life could be so simple.

468
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:44,774
Good.

469
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:46,067
Okay, New York.

470
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:50,864
Show me how it's done.
Where do you see yourself in five years?

471
00:24:50,947 --> 00:24:54,367
Oh, please. That's too easy.
About to graduate Princeton.

472
00:24:54,451 --> 00:24:56,745
Okay, I should've figured.

473
00:24:56,828 --> 00:24:58,413
Yeah.

474
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:01,124
I think I can do this now.

475
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:04,127
See? I knew it.

476
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:07,172
By being prepared,
you can get everything you want.

477
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:08,965
Everything, huh?

478
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:15,472
Everybody deserves to dream big,
especially my friends.

479
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:16,806
Like you.

480
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:19,684
Right.

481
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:26,399
-Hi.
-Hey, Grace.

482
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:28,151
-Hey.
-Have you seen Jackie anywhere?

483
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:30,445
Yeah, I think
she's still on the road with Cole. Yeah.

484
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:31,404
With Cole?

485
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:35,700
Uh, yeah.
I mean, the rep's car broke down.

486
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:38,078
Um, it's for sure like
a student-teacher thing.

487
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:42,374
You know, uh, the boring aesthetic
of cardigan sweaters and corduroy.

488
00:25:43,124 --> 00:25:45,835
Okay, I'll just text her then.

489
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:46,753
Okay.

490
00:25:47,587 --> 00:25:48,421
Yeah.

491
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:53,301
And I've been assistant coaching
my school's team ever since.

492
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:56,137
There aren't a lot of high schoolers
who can handle leading their peers.

493
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:57,472
It's not always easy.

494
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:03,103
Thank you for, uh, agreeing to do this.

495
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:05,939
Least I could do. Thanks for your help.

496
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:07,440
Sure.

497
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:09,317
Now, uh, I've got another question.

498
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:13,238
How would your friends describe you?

499
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,241
Um…

500
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:21,121
I think

501
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:25,917
that I'm a lot different
from the guy I was a year ago,

502
00:26:26,001 --> 00:26:27,961
in that I don't always get things right.

503
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:32,173
But when I don't,
I try my best to fix them.

504
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:34,759
That's great to hear.

505
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:37,304
We look for more than just perfect grades.

506
00:26:37,887 --> 00:26:40,390
Resilience and determination
can go a long way.

507
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:43,810
Oh no. Already?

508
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:48,648
And as far as this bad boy goes,
I think she's looking pretty good.

509
00:26:48,732 --> 00:26:49,566
Okay.

510
00:26:49,649 --> 00:26:54,487
Let me just do one more thing,
and then you should be good to go.

511
00:26:55,488 --> 00:26:57,240
-Thank you.
-You got it.

512
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:10,462
I know you're not interested
in community college.

513
00:27:11,546 --> 00:27:15,216
No. But I am interested in apologizing

514
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,969
to the girl who wants
to go to community college.

515
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:25,352
Apologizing for…

516
00:27:26,811 --> 00:27:27,687
Not listening.

517
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:30,690
I just figured you loved acting
as much as I did.

518
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:32,233
And it was wrong.

519
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:36,071
And I totally get why
we aren't together anymore.

520
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:40,075
Danny, couples fight all the time.
Doesn't mean we're broken up.

521
00:27:41,284 --> 00:27:43,662
Unless… you want to be.

522
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:44,871
No.

523
00:27:44,954 --> 00:27:46,873
No. No, absolutely not.

524
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:47,791
Good.

525
00:27:47,874 --> 00:27:49,376
Then apology accepted.

526
00:27:51,419 --> 00:27:55,507
Like I said, drama club was fun,
but acting's a long shot.

527
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,008
I feel pretty good about my odds.

528
00:27:57,092 --> 00:27:58,093
I know.

529
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:01,513
I just… I don't want to see you get hurt.

530
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:05,475
I just think it's better
to be more realistic.

531
00:28:05,558 --> 00:28:07,268
So I'm unrealistic?

532
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:09,604
You know that's not what I mean.

533
00:28:10,730 --> 00:28:12,148
You know what is realistic?

534
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:16,611
Applying to business schools in New York
to see if you could get in.

535
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:20,156
Applications are expensive.
I told you, I… I can't afford it.

536
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,242
Well, fee waivers exist.

537
00:28:22,826 --> 00:28:24,744
Scholarships exist. You could try.

538
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:27,622
Danny, I can't make plans
that revolve around you.

539
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:30,917
I have to do what's best for me.
Like I said, I have a plan.

540
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:34,212
Yeah, but we could've tried
to plan together.

541
00:28:35,463 --> 00:28:39,008
Instead, you've just completely
shut me out of your future.

542
00:28:41,928 --> 00:28:45,557
I didn't know we had an expiration date,
but apparently we do.

543
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:48,268
Danny.

544
00:29:00,029 --> 00:29:02,866
-Did you hear that?
-Yeah, it went really well.

545
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:04,409
I even asked him about my grades.

546
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:07,328
And he said my coaching experience
could help make up for it.

547
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:09,205
Just glad to see you so happy.

548
00:29:11,040 --> 00:29:13,626
Whoa, hey. Everything okay?

549
00:29:14,794 --> 00:29:16,755
I'm going to miss
my final mock driving run.

550
00:29:16,838 --> 00:29:18,715
Oh, Jackie, I'm… I'm sorry.

551
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:22,010
Don't worry about it.
I'll ask Coach Allen to make it up.

552
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:25,472
Uh, wait. Wait.
How about a little practice now?

553
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:27,974
Ha ha, very funny.

554
00:29:28,057 --> 00:29:28,975
I'm serious.

555
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:31,394
-I've never driven a stick shift before.
-Oh, please.

556
00:29:31,478 --> 00:29:33,354
You'll be fine. I'll… I'll teach you.

557
00:29:33,438 --> 00:29:34,939
I'll teach you. Come on.

558
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:36,816
Come on.

559
00:29:46,701 --> 00:29:48,828
Do you think this should be
the cover photo?

560
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:51,331
Come on, we can't use that photo.

561
00:29:51,414 --> 00:29:53,917
I just want everyone
to see you the way that I do.

562
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:58,004
The hottest, coolest, sweetest guy ever.

563
00:30:00,757 --> 00:30:04,594
Zach, did something happen
between you and Skylar?

564
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:07,013
Did he say something to you?

565
00:30:08,765 --> 00:30:12,936
Look, just because he didn't give you
the attention you deserved and lost you--

566
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:14,020
What was it?

567
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:18,066
Okay.

568
00:30:19,734 --> 00:30:21,611
Okay, yes. Um…

569
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:28,159
Yeah. Something did happen
between me and Skylar.

570
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:31,746
My sophomore year.

571
00:30:32,288 --> 00:30:33,498
I hadn't come out yet.

572
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:38,253
But Skylar and I started hooking up.

573
00:30:40,338 --> 00:30:43,633
But after a while,
he was just always so busy.

574
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:49,222
I mean, it was always
Student Council or the paper.

575
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:52,392
I mean, that's why I joined,
so I could get closer to him.

576
00:30:52,475 --> 00:30:55,937
But no matter what I did
to try and get him to focus on me,

577
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,897
he was always busy.

578
00:30:57,981 --> 00:30:59,107
And finally,

579
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:03,361
he told me that he wanted
to be with somebody who was out.

580
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:06,990
And so I came out.

581
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:08,908
Eventually.

582
00:31:10,159 --> 00:31:11,911
But you two were already together.

583
00:31:14,664 --> 00:31:15,957
So wait, are you…

584
00:31:17,458 --> 00:31:21,170
Are you just trying to get back at Skylar,
or are you trying to get back with him?

585
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:22,672
No.

586
00:31:23,381 --> 00:31:24,883
No, Nathan.

587
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:27,385
I didn't think the past mattered.

588
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:30,305
It doesn't matter.

589
00:31:35,226 --> 00:31:36,060
It…

590
00:31:36,686 --> 00:31:37,770
Yeah, it does.

591
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:52,869
Is Jackie coming?

592
00:31:57,332 --> 00:32:00,793
I know I don't have to tell you
that there's no texting and driving.

593
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:03,087
Let's go.

594
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:06,883
She's on her way.

595
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:25,818
You know, after work,
my hardworking, seven-months-pregnant wife

596
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:29,864
looks forward to dinner
that I make for her on the table by 6:30.

597
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:31,866
You mind doing the speed limit, buddy?

598
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:33,868
I can't do that.

599
00:32:34,452 --> 00:32:35,828
-Excuse me?
-Sorry.

600
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:41,042
It's just, uh, Jackie's busy
with college fair stuff,

601
00:32:41,125 --> 00:32:43,628
and I know how much
this final run means to her,

602
00:32:43,711 --> 00:32:45,213
so I can't go any faster.

603
00:32:45,713 --> 00:32:48,883
All right. We'll wait
a little longer for her.

604
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:56,933
Okay. Easy, eyes on the road.

605
00:33:03,481 --> 00:33:04,774
-Okay.
-Perfect.

606
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:06,484
Now for the highway.

607
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:07,568
Are you serious?

608
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:09,195
Yes. You've got this.

609
00:33:12,156 --> 00:33:12,991
Okay.

610
00:33:21,457 --> 00:33:23,793
Just feel the car as you go. Right?

611
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:25,795
Foot on the clutch.

612
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:30,717
Take it easy.

613
00:33:31,926 --> 00:33:33,094
Ready to shift.

614
00:33:34,262 --> 00:33:35,930
Good. Now.

615
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,607
A little more gentle.

616
00:33:47,400 --> 00:33:49,193
-You're gonna have to shift again.
-I got it.

617
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:00,455
Come in.

618
00:34:03,207 --> 00:34:04,250
Hi, Katherine.

619
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:06,544
What you doing here, Richard?

620
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:08,713
I wanted to talk to you.

621
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:14,260
I'm sorry about your chicken coop.

622
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:15,470
Hmm.

623
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:20,475
Not sorry about cutting George and I
out of decisions or sidelining Will?

624
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:23,227
We needed to see
a return on the investment quickly

625
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:24,979
and to speed things up.

626
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:27,273
The investors need clarity
and decisiveness,

627
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:29,650
and you know George
has been dragging his feet.

628
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:33,821
And Will has always been a junior partner,
and he is great. He is.

629
00:34:34,322 --> 00:34:37,366
But he needs direction.
He's never done this before.

630
00:34:37,450 --> 00:34:40,620
I understand
that our financial situation isn't great

631
00:34:40,703 --> 00:34:42,330
and that we have to get this done.

632
00:34:43,748 --> 00:34:46,375
But pushing this through
at the expense of my husband and my son,

633
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:47,794
that's not gonna fly with me.

634
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:50,630
You don't get to make that choice
when it's other people's money!

635
00:34:54,926 --> 00:34:57,345
How much of your own money
did you invest in this, Richard?

636
00:34:58,262 --> 00:35:00,389
-You don't need to worry about that.
-Well, I am now.

637
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:10,608
I couldn't convince my business partners
to invest the amount we needed,

638
00:35:10,691 --> 00:35:13,069
so I made up the difference
with my own money.

639
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:16,906
-I used my apartment as collateral.
-Oh.

640
00:35:16,989 --> 00:35:18,157
-I…
-Oh my God.

641
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:21,953
…figured if I got involved with the ranch,

642
00:35:22,036 --> 00:35:24,831
that I could save Jackie's home
here in Silver Falls too

643
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:26,874
and spend more time with her.

644
00:35:28,501 --> 00:35:30,419
She's all the family I have left.

645
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:36,759
And I wanted her to feel settled
and to feel safe.

646
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:41,556
She doesn't need
any more upheaval in her life.

647
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:44,767
And I understand that, Richard.
I really do.

648
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:52,191
You didn't have to take on so much risk.
I mean, we could've found another way.

649
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:53,276
Could you?

650
00:35:53,359 --> 00:35:54,527
We always have.

651
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:56,863
Here's what you need to know.

652
00:35:57,405 --> 00:36:01,284
You will always have a place in my home
because you're family now too.

653
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,870
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

654
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:05,204
Can you do me one favor?

655
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:07,206
Are you gonna push your luck?

656
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:11,252
Let me tell George.

657
00:36:11,335 --> 00:36:12,879
He should hear it from me.

658
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:17,341
I can do that.

659
00:36:19,802 --> 00:36:20,803
Thanks.

660
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:26,017
-You're late.
-I know. I'm sorry.

661
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:29,228
Luckily, Alex had
a very convincing argument on your behalf,

662
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:31,272
so I'll give you the benefit of the doubt.

663
00:36:31,355 --> 00:36:32,565
Let's get moving.

664
00:36:44,577 --> 00:36:48,497
That was cool of you to get
Coach Allen to stick around for her.

665
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:51,709
It's nothing.

666
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:56,589
Meeting go okay?

667
00:36:57,798 --> 00:36:58,633
Yeah.

668
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:01,093
I think so.

669
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:05,223
Good.

670
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:11,562
Skylar?

671
00:37:13,522 --> 00:37:14,565
What do you want?

672
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:17,902
I wanted to talk to you
about what happened with Nathan.

673
00:37:17,985 --> 00:37:19,654
What is there to talk about?

674
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:22,740
You stole my boyfriend
just to prove you could.

675
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:24,617
No, that wasn't it.

676
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:26,244
Then what is it?

677
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:29,830
Is it because we broke up?
Are you still upset about that?

678
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:32,291
Of course I am. I--

679
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:36,587
We were just in different places, Zach.
It wasn't anything more than that.

680
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:38,589
We're not in different places anymore.

681
00:37:40,716 --> 00:37:43,052
I'm out. We're both single.

682
00:37:43,135 --> 00:37:44,178
What?

683
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:46,847
Nathan and I, we're not together anymore.

684
00:37:47,348 --> 00:37:49,475
Are you serious?

685
00:37:51,102 --> 00:37:53,562
You're unbelievable. You know that?

686
00:37:54,689 --> 00:37:56,524
Look, Skylar, I…

687
00:37:57,817 --> 00:37:59,443
I like Nathan and all, but…

688
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:04,407
Honestly, I just wanted
to get your attention.

689
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:06,409
Well, you got that.

690
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:07,576
Sky!

691
00:38:08,869 --> 00:38:09,704
I miss you.

692
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:11,580
So what are you saying?

693
00:38:11,664 --> 00:38:13,624
I want you back, Sky.

694
00:38:23,509 --> 00:38:26,345
I didn't know you were still up.
I thought everyone was asleep.

695
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:28,306
They are.

696
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:32,935
I just wanted to say thank you
for holding off Coach Allen.

697
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:35,938
Ah, yeah. He wasn't happy about it.

698
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:38,274
But I knew how much
you wanted to practice.

699
00:38:38,357 --> 00:38:40,109
You're lucky he didn't make you run laps.

700
00:38:40,192 --> 00:38:42,069
Oh, well, he was this close.

701
00:38:44,405 --> 00:38:45,364
I, uh…

702
00:38:46,741 --> 00:38:48,451
I need to apologize.

703
00:38:49,076 --> 00:38:49,910
For what?

704
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:53,622
I should've told you that I was
skipping school with Cole and I…

705
00:38:53,706 --> 00:38:55,875
Jackie. Do I need to be jealous?

706
00:38:55,958 --> 00:38:57,251
Of course not.

707
00:38:57,335 --> 00:38:59,462
Absolutely not.

708
00:38:59,545 --> 00:39:00,713
Then it's all good.

709
00:39:02,381 --> 00:39:04,175
-Seriously?
-Seriously.

710
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:11,807
And I should've said it the other day.

711
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,061
But I love you too.

712
00:39:19,106 --> 00:39:22,651
I'll be right here

713
00:39:23,152 --> 00:39:24,862
Till you're steady

714
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:29,742
I'll be right here

715
00:39:30,242 --> 00:39:31,827
When it's heavy

716
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:39,502
All right.

717
00:39:40,086 --> 00:39:42,421
Are you taller than me now?
Goodness gracious.

718
00:39:43,089 --> 00:39:43,923
Mm-hmm.

719
00:39:44,006 --> 00:39:45,508
-…a bit rehearsed.
-Coach!

720
00:39:45,591 --> 00:39:47,676
-Cole, hold on a second.
-What's up?

721
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:49,553
I didn't want to put
any added pressure on you,

722
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:51,722
but, uh, I know the coach back at UT.

723
00:39:51,806 --> 00:39:54,266
And they don't usually send reps
to Silver Falls,

724
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:56,519
but I told them they needed to meet you.

725
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:57,520
What?

726
00:39:58,354 --> 00:39:59,522
Thank you, Coach.

727
00:39:59,605 --> 00:40:01,899
Yeah. Hey, you… you deserved it.

728
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:04,443
And the rep had a ton to say about you.

729
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:06,737
He loved you.

730
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:09,657
He said he's gonna do his best
come admission-decision time.

731
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:11,117
Thank you, Coach. I…

732
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:13,911
If I get in, um, um, I won't let you down.

733
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:15,621
No, when you get in.

734
00:40:16,622 --> 00:40:19,208
All right, let's go. I got an announcement
I gotta make to the team.

735
00:40:19,291 --> 00:40:21,836
Whoa. You don't…
you don't have to tell them.

736
00:40:23,379 --> 00:40:25,089
If only that was it.

737
00:40:28,426 --> 00:40:29,260
What?

738
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:32,596
All right, team. Put your shirts back on.

739
00:40:33,764 --> 00:40:34,807
Thought we had practice.

740
00:40:34,890 --> 00:40:36,892
Unfortunately, the Lockwood soccer team

741
00:40:36,976 --> 00:40:39,937
snuck into the weed shop with fake IDs

742
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:42,440
and got higher
than the fireworks on the 4th of July.

743
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:44,984
So now every team in the area
has to take a drug test.

744
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:49,363
But, no, don't worry.
It's just standard. It's all very fair.

745
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:51,657
Even Coach Walter has to take one too.

746
00:40:52,408 --> 00:40:55,119
Okay, you two. Let's go. You're up.

747
00:40:59,915 --> 00:41:03,377
Dude, there's no way I'm gonna pass.
I smoked that joint at the rodeo.

748
00:41:03,461 --> 00:41:06,088
If you test positive,
you'll miss a couple games.

749
00:41:06,172 --> 00:41:07,548
You wanna tell my dad that?

750
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:10,301
No, I… I… I guess not.

751
00:41:10,384 --> 00:41:11,427
Okay, um…

752
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:13,971
But you haven't been smoking, right?

753
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:17,850
-No.
-Okay, so you can take the test for me.

754
00:41:18,767 --> 00:41:19,852
What?

755
00:41:19,935 --> 00:41:22,146
We can sneak some of your sample
and use it as mine.

756
00:41:22,229 --> 00:41:24,773
Coach Allen probably lends you
his office keys all the time.

757
00:41:25,357 --> 00:41:27,651
-We'd get caught.
